IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- section 3: law and equity to be administered concurrently.
--
-- The chapeau of s 3 limits every rule that follows to "every civil cause or matter commenced in the court".
-- Each limb function therefore takes that fact as its first input; when it is FALSE the answer is NOTHING (a scope
-- limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (c)).
-- Each limb is a direction to the court.  What it means for a claimant or defendant is the right to the relief,
-- effect or order the limb names.  The open-textured antecedent of each limb (what equity would have given before
-- 1 January 1879) is one plain yes/no input; the Act is not asked to be re-run through pre-1879 equity.

§ `Section 3 -- the chapeau and the rules following`

-- src:104 | 3. In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court, law and
-- src:105 | equity shall be administered by the court in its original jurisdiction
-- src:106 | and by the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of
-- src:107 | Appeal according to the rules following:
@ref s 3 chapeau (src:104-107)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 law and equity are administered concurrently in the cause or matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"

-- src:111 | (a) if any claimant claims to be entitled to any equitable estate
-- src:112 | or right, or to relief upon any equitable ground against any
-- src:113 | deed, instrument or contract, or against any right, title or
-- src:114 | claim whatsoever asserted by any defendant in such cause
-- src:115 | or matter, or to any relief founded upon a legal right, which
-- src:116 | before 1 January 1879 could only have been given by the
-- src:117 | court on its equity side, the court shall give to such
-- src:118 | claimant such and the same relief, as ought to have been
-- src:119 | given by the court, on its equity side, in a suit or proceeding
-- src:120 | for the same, or the like purpose, properly instituted before
-- src:121 | that date;
@ref s 3(a) (src:111-121)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant claims an equitable estate or right or relief on an equitable ground against a deed instrument or contract or against a right title or claim asserted by the defendant or relief founded on a legal right which before 1 January 1879 could only have been given on the equity side` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(a) the court shall give the claimant the relief that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"
        IF `the claimant claims an equitable estate or right or relief on an equitable ground against a deed instrument or contract or against a right title or claim asserted by the defendant or relief founded on a legal right which before 1 January 1879 could only have been given on the equity side` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if any claimant claims to be entitled to any equitable estate or right" -- the limb gives the claimant nothing for a claim outside its description

-- src:127 | (b) if any defendant claims to be entitled to any equitable
-- src:128 | estate or right, or to relief upon any equitable ground
-- src:129 | against any deed, instrument or contract, or against any
-- src:130 | right, title or claim asserted by any claimant in such cause
-- src:131 | or matter, or alleges any ground of equitable defence to any
-- src:132 | claim of the claimant in such cause or matter, the court
-- src:133 | shall give to every equitable estate, right or ground of relief
-- src:134 | so claimed, and to every equitable defence so alleged, such
-- src:135 | and the same effect, by way of defence against the claim of
-- src:136 | such claimant, as the court on its equity side ought to have
-- src:137 | given, if the same or the like matters had been relied on by
-- src:138 | way of defence, in any suit or proceeding instituted in the
-- src:139 | court on its equity side, for the same or the like purpose,
-- src:140 | before 1 January 1879;
@ref s 3(b) (src:127-140)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant claims an equitable estate or right or relief on an equitable ground against a deed instrument or contract or against a right title or claim asserted by the claimant or alleges a ground of equitable defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(b) the court shall give the equitable right or defence the effect that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"
        IF `the defendant claims an equitable estate or right or relief on an equitable ground against a deed instrument or contract or against a right title or claim asserted by the claimant or alleges a ground of equitable defence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if any defendant claims to be entitled to any equitable estate or right"

-- src:150 | (c) the court may also grant to any defendant, in respect of any
-- src:151 | equitable estate or right, or other matter of equity, and also
-- src:152 | in respect of any legal estate, right or title claimed or
-- src:153 | asserted by him, all such relief against any claimant, as
-- src:154 | such defendant shall have properly claimed by his
-- src:155 | pleading, and as the court might have granted in any suit
-- src:156 | instituted for that purpose, by the same defendant against
-- src:157 | the same claimant before 1 January 1879 and also all such
-- src:158 | relief, relating to or connected with the original subject of
-- src:159 | the cause or matter, and in like manner claimed against any
-- src:160 | other person, whether already a party to the same cause or
-- src:161 | matter or not, who has been duly served with notice in
-- src:162 | writing of such claim, pursuant to the Rules of Court, as
-- src:163 | might properly have been granted against such person, if
-- src:164 | he had been made a defendant to a cause, duly instituted by
-- src:165 | the same defendant for the like purpose; and every person
-- src:166 | served with any such notice shall thenceforth be deemed a
-- src:167 | party to such cause or matter, with the same rights, in
-- src:168 | respect of his defence against such claim, as if he had been
-- src:169 | duly sued in the ordinary way by such defendant;
@ref s 3(c) (src:150-169)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has properly claimed the relief by the defendant's pleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relief is of a kind the court might have granted in a suit instituted for that purpose by the same defendant against the same claimant before 1 January 1879 or relates to or is connected with the original subject of the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(c) the court may grant the defendant relief against the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"
        IF `the defendant has properly claimed the relief by the defendant's pleading` AND `the relief is of a kind the court might have granted in a suit instituted for that purpose by the same defendant against the same claimant before 1 January 1879 or relates to or is connected with the original subject of the cause or matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as such defendant shall have properly claimed by his pleading"

-- src:160 | other person, whether already a party to the same cause or
-- src:161 | matter or not, who has been duly served with notice in
-- src:162 | writing of such claim, pursuant to the Rules of Court, as
-- src:163 | might properly have been granted against such person, if
-- src:164 | he had been made a defendant to a cause, duly instituted by
-- src:165 | the same defendant for the like purpose; and every person
-- src:166 | served with any such notice shall thenceforth be deemed a
-- src:167 | party to such cause or matter, with the same rights, in
-- src:168 | respect of his defence against such claim, as if he had been
-- src:169 | duly sued in the ordinary way by such defendant;
@ref s 3(c) the person served with notice (src:160-169)
GIVEN `the person has been duly served with notice in writing of the claim pursuant to the Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(c) the person served with notice of the claim is deemed a party to the cause or matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has been duly served with notice in writing of the claim pursuant to the Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every person served with any such notice shall thenceforth be deemed a party"

-- src:175 | (d) the court shall recognise and take notice of all equitable
-- src:176 | estates, titles and rights, and all equitable duties and
-- src:177 | liabilities, appearing incidentally in the course of any cause
-- src:178 | or matter, in the same manner in which the court on its
-- src:179 | equity side would have recognised and taken notice of the
-- src:180 | same, in any suit or proceeding duly instituted therein
-- src:181 | before 1 January 1879;
@ref s 3(d) (src:175-181)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equitable estate title right duty or liability appears incidentally in the course of the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equity side would have recognised and taken notice of it in a suit or proceeding duly instituted before 1 January 1879` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(d) the court shall recognise and take notice of the equitable estate title right duty or liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"
        IF `the equitable estate title right duty or liability appears incidentally in the course of the cause or matter` AND `the equity side would have recognised and taken notice of it in a suit or proceeding duly instituted before 1 January 1879` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appearing incidentally in the course of any cause or matter"

-- src:185 | (e) no cause or proceeding at any time pending in the court in
-- src:186 | its original jurisdiction or in the Appellate Division of the
-- src:187 | High Court or the Court of Appeal, shall be restrained by
-- src:188 | prohibition or injunction; but every matter of equity on
-- src:193 | which an injunction against the prosecution of any such
-- src:194 | cause or proceeding might have been obtained if the Civil
-- src:195 | Law Ordinance 1878 (IV/1878) had not been passed, either
-- src:196 | unconditionally or on any terms or conditions, may be
-- src:197 | relied on by way of defence thereto;
@ref s 3(e) (src:185-197)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause or proceeding is pending in the court in its original jurisdiction or in the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(e) the pending cause or proceeding may be restrained by prohibition or injunction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"
        IF `the cause or proceeding is pending in the court in its original jurisdiction or in the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of Appeal` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no cause or proceeding at any time pending in the court ... shall be restrained by prohibition or injunction"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no cause or proceeding at any time pending in the court in its original jurisdiction or in the Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of Appeal"

-- src:188 | prohibition or injunction; but every matter of equity on
-- src:193 | which an injunction against the prosecution of any such
-- src:194 | cause or proceeding might have been obtained if the Civil
-- src:195 | Law Ordinance 1878 (IV/1878) had not been passed, either
-- src:196 | unconditionally or on any terms or conditions, may be
-- src:197 | relied on by way of defence thereto;
@ref s 3(e) a matter of equity relied on by way of defence (src:188-197)
GIVEN `the matter is a matter of equity on which an injunction against the prosecution of the cause or proceeding might have been obtained either unconditionally or on terms or conditions if the Civil Law Ordinance 1878 had not been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(e) the matter of equity may be relied on by way of defence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is a matter of equity on which an injunction against the prosecution of the cause or proceeding might have been obtained either unconditionally or on terms or conditions if the Civil Law Ordinance 1878 had not been passed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every matter of equity on which an injunction ... might have been obtained"

-- src:201 | (f) nothing in this Act shall disable the court from directing a
-- src:202 | stay of proceedings in any cause or matter pending before
-- src:203 | it, if it thinks fit; and any person, whether a party or not to
-- src:204 | any such cause or matter, who would have been entitled if
-- src:205 | the Civil Law Ordinance 1878 had not been passed, to
-- src:206 | apply to the court to restrain the prosecution thereof, or
-- src:207 | who may be entitled to enforce, by attachment or
-- src:208 | otherwise, any judgment, decree, rule or order, contrary
-- src:209 | to which all or any part of the proceedings in such cause or
-- src:210 | matter may have been taken, may apply to the court, by
-- src:211 | summons in a summary way, for a stay of proceedings in
-- src:212 | such cause or matter, either generally, or so far as is
-- src:213 | necessary for the purpose of justice; and the court shall
-- src:214 | thereupon make such order as is just;
@ref s 3(f) (src:201-214)
GIVEN `the court is directing a stay of proceedings in a cause or matter pending before it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(f) this Act disables the court from directing a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court is directing a stay of proceedings in a cause or matter pending before it` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this Act shall disable the court from directing a stay of proceedings"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limb speaks only of a stay in a cause or matter pending before the court

-- src:204 | any such cause or matter, who would have been entitled if
-- src:205 | the Civil Law Ordinance 1878 had not been passed, to
-- src:206 | apply to the court to restrain the prosecution thereof, or
-- src:207 | who may be entitled to enforce, by attachment or
-- src:208 | otherwise, any judgment, decree, rule or order, contrary
-- src:209 | to which all or any part of the proceedings in such cause or
-- src:210 | matter may have been taken, may apply to the court, by
-- src:211 | summons in a summary way, for a stay of proceedings in
-- src:212 | such cause or matter, either generally, or so far as is
-- src:213 | necessary for the purpose of justice; and the court shall
-- src:214 | thereupon make such order as is just;
@ref s 3(f) application for a stay (src:204-214)
GIVEN `the person would have been entitled if the Civil Law Ordinance 1878 had not been passed to apply to the court to restrain the prosecution of the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person may be entitled to enforce by attachment or otherwise a judgment decree rule or order contrary to which part of the proceedings may have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(f) the person may apply to the court by summons in a summary way for a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person would have been entitled if the Civil Law Ordinance 1878 had not been passed to apply to the court to restrain the prosecution of the cause or matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person may be entitled to enforce by attachment or otherwise a judgment decree rule or order contrary to which part of the proceedings may have been taken` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person, whether a party or not ... who would have been entitled ... or who may be entitled"

-- src:213 | necessary for the purpose of justice; and the court shall
-- src:214 | thereupon make such order as is just;
@ref s 3(f) the order (src:213-214)
GIVEN `a person has applied by summons in a summary way for a stay of proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(f) the court shall thereupon make such order as is just` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a person has applied by summons in a summary way for a stay of proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "thereupon", on the application

-- src:219 | (g) subject to the aforesaid provisions for giving effect to
-- src:220 | equitable rights and other matters of equity in the manner
-- src:221 | aforesaid, the said court shall recognise and give effect to
-- src:222 | all legal claims and demands, and all estates, titles, rights,
-- src:223 | duties, obligations and liabilities by the common law or by
-- src:224 | any custom, or created by any law having force in
-- src:225 | Singapore, in the same manner as the same would have
-- src:226 | been recognised and given effect to if this Act had not been
-- src:227 | passed;
@ref s 3(g) (src:219-227)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal claim demand estate title right duty obligation or liability arises by the common law or by a custom or is created by a law having force in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(g) the court shall recognise and give effect to the legal claim estate title right duty obligation or liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"
        IF `the legal claim demand estate title right duty obligation or liability arises by the common law or by a custom or is created by a law having force in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the common law or by any custom, or created by any law having force in Singapore"

-- src:236 | (h) the court in the exercise of its original jurisdiction and the
-- src:237 | Appellate Division of the High Court or the Court of
-- src:238 | Appeal, in every cause or matter pending before it, shall
-- src:239 | grant, either absolutely or on such reasonable terms and
-- src:240 | conditions as to it seems just, all such remedies whatsoever
-- src:241 | as any of the parties thereto appear to be entitled to, in
-- src:242 | respect of any and every legal or equitable claim properly
-- src:243 | brought forward by them respectively in such cause or
-- src:244 | matter; so that, as far as possible, all matters so in
-- src:245 | controversy between the said parties respectively may be
-- src:246 | completely and finally determined, and all multiplicity of
-- src:247 | legal proceedings concerning any of such matters avoided.
@ref s 3(h) (src:236-247)
GIVEN `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party appears to be entitled to the remedy in respect of a legal or equitable claim properly brought forward by that party in the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(h) the court shall grant the remedy either absolutely or on reasonable terms and conditions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause or matter is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in every cause or matter pending before it"
        IF `the party appears to be entitled to the remedy in respect of a legal or equitable claim properly brought forward by that party in the cause or matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any and every legal or equitable claim properly brought forward by them"

§§ `Section 3 -- tests`

-- chapeau
#ASSERT `s 3 law and equity are administered concurrently in the cause or matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "every civil cause or matter commenced in the court"
#ASSERT `s 3 law and equity are administered concurrently in the cause or matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a cause not commenced in the court: the chapeau is silent
-- (a)
#ASSERT `s 3(a) the court shall give the claimant the relief that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "the court shall give to such claimant such and the same relief"
#ASSERT `s 3(a) the court shall give the claimant the relief that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a claim outside the description
#ASSERT `s 3(a) the court shall give the claimant the relief that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a cause commenced in the court
-- (b)
#ASSERT `s 3(b) the court shall give the equitable right or defence the effect that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "such and the same effect, by way of defence"
#ASSERT `s 3(b) the court shall give the equitable right or defence the effect that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no equitable defence alleged
-- (c)
#ASSERT `s 3(c) the court may grant the defendant relief against the claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "the court may also grant to any defendant ... all such relief"
#ASSERT `s 3(c) the court may grant the defendant relief against the claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not "properly claimed by his pleading"
#ASSERT `s 3(c) the person served with notice of the claim is deemed a party to the cause or matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall thenceforth be deemed a party"
#ASSERT `s 3(c) the person served with notice of the claim is deemed a party to the cause or matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not served with notice
-- (d)
#ASSERT `s 3(d) the court shall recognise and take notice of the equitable estate title right duty or liability` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall recognise and take notice of all equitable estates"
#ASSERT `s 3(d) the court shall recognise and take notice of the equitable estate title right duty or liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- it does not appear incidentally
-- (e)
#ASSERT `s 3(e) the pending cause or proceeding may be restrained by prohibition or injunction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall be restrained by prohibition or injunction" is denied
#ASSERT `s 3(e) the pending cause or proceeding may be restrained by prohibition or injunction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not pending in those courts
#ASSERT `s 3(e) the matter of equity may be relied on by way of defence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may be relied on by way of defence thereto"
#ASSERT `s 3(e) the matter of equity may be relied on by way of defence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not such a matter of equity
-- (f)
#ASSERT `s 3(f) this Act disables the court from directing a stay of proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "nothing in this Act shall disable the court"
#ASSERT `s 3(f) this Act disables the court from directing a stay of proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a stay in a pending cause
#ASSERT `s 3(f) the person may apply to the court by summons in a summary way for a stay of proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- would have been entitled to apply to restrain
#ASSERT `s 3(f) the person may apply to the court by summons in a summary way for a stay of proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- may be entitled to enforce a judgment
#ASSERT `s 3(f) the person may apply to the court by summons in a summary way for a stay of proceedings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- neither
#ASSERT `s 3(f) the court shall thereupon make such order as is just` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "the court shall thereupon make such order as is just"
#ASSERT `s 3(f) the court shall thereupon make such order as is just` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no application made
-- (g)
#ASSERT `s 3(g) the court shall recognise and give effect to the legal claim estate title right duty obligation or liability` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall recognise and give effect to all legal claims and demands"
#ASSERT `s 3(g) the court shall recognise and give effect to the legal claim estate title right duty obligation or liability` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not from the common law, custom or a law in force
-- (h)
#ASSERT `s 3(h) the court shall grant the remedy either absolutely or on reasonable terms and conditions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall grant ... all such remedies whatsoever as any of the parties thereto appear to be entitled to"
#ASSERT `s 3(h) the court shall grant the remedy either absolutely or on reasonable terms and conditions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the party does not appear entitled
#ASSERT `s 3(h) the court shall grant the remedy either absolutely or on reasonable terms and conditions` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a cause pending before the court
